The largest concentration is in Migjorn Province, where communities are found along the southern coast in fishing villages and small towns. These are the most culturally distinct, maintaining Dagiti language traditions, Anitist religious practices, and maritime customs. The Migjorn Fosian Liba are predominantly working-class, employed in fishing, agriculture, and the service sector.

In Estret Province, the population is concentrated in [[Sant Cristòfor]], primarily in the working-class ''ciutats'' of [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]] and [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]]. The Estret Fosian Liba are more assimilated, with higher rates of intermarriage and lower rates of Dagiti language retention. A small community also exists in [[Portnou]], dating from the colonial era.

=== Relationship to Nou-Dagiti ===

The Fosian Liba are distinct from more recent Dagit immigrants, known as [[Nou-Dagiti Balboan people|Nou-Dagiti Balboans]], who have arrived since the 1990s drawn by Balboa's economic growth. Despite sharing a broad North Fosian ancestral region, the two communities have little social interaction and do not significantly intermix. The University of Sant Cristòfor study found that the Fosian Liba's ancestral origins were distributed across the Balausia Peninsula and not exclusively from the Republic of Dagit, complicating the implied connection between the two communities.

